        "execSummary":  "As enterprise AI spending scales, the gap between organizations that model their inference costs and those that default to managed APIs is becoming a significant budget liability. Linthicum\u0027s core decision rule — serverless favors variable workloads, dedicated compute favors steady-state — is actionable guidance for any team running production AI at scale. For customer-support leaders with consistent, high-volume AI inference (e.g., always-on agent assist), dedicated compute or reserved capacity may deliver materially better economics than per-call API pricing. The caveat is operational overhead: serverless trades cost efficiency for management simplicity, and not every team has the MLOps maturity to manage dedicated inference infrastructure.",
