        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "This article presents a framework for managing AI agent memory through lifecycle policies on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. Three complementary strategies — TTL-based expiration, relevance decay scoring, and LLM-based consolidation — are orchestrated via AWS Step Functions to automatically prune and consolidate agent memories on a nightly schedule. The approach prevents memory bloat while preserving contextually important information over long agent lifecycles.",
        "execSummary":  "As enterprise AI agents are deployed in production, unmanaged memory accumulation becomes a real operational cost and accuracy risk — this article offers a production-ready framework for automated memory governance using AWS-native tooling. The three-pronged approach (expiration, decay, consolidation) mirrors how human organizations manage institutional knowledge: prune the stale, downweight the irrelevant, and compress the durable. For customer support and operational AI use cases where agents persist context across weeks or months, this is a non-trivial architectural concern that most teams are not yet solving systematically. The dependency on AWS Step Functions and Bedrock AgentCore means organizations on other clouds or with hybrid architectures will need to translate these patterns to their own orchestration layer.",
