        "date":  "2026-09-04",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Intuit developed an AI-powered disaster recovery assistant using Amazon Bedrock that automates failover decisions for microservices across multiple AWS regions. The system encodes operational knowledge as typed \u0027skills\u0027 and uses a bounded agentic loop where foundation models determine actions while conventional code deterministically executes them. This approach reduces recovery times and eliminates reliance on individual engineer expertise during outages.",
        "execSummary":  "Intuit\u0027s production deployment of an agentic DR assistant represents one of the clearest enterprise case studies yet for AI in high-stakes operational automation — the agent handles multi-region failover decisions that previously required senior engineer judgment under pressure. The bounded agentic loop design — AI decides, deterministic code executes — is the right architectural pattern for enterprises that cannot tolerate hallucinated actions in production, and it is a model worth adopting broadly in IT ops. For enterprise leaders, the key takeaway is that agentic AI can compress mean-time-to-recovery and de-risk key-person dependencies in critical infrastructure. The caveat: this architecture requires significant upfront work to encode operational knowledge as typed skills, which is a non-trivial organizational and engineering investment.",
