        "summary":  "The article demonstrates how to build AI-driven development workflows using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore through two practical implementations: automated Mermaid ER diagram generation from SQL schemas and multi-agent code security analysis. These systems illustrate patterns for integrating AI as a collaborator throughout the software development lifecycle while maintaining human oversight. The multi-agent security analysis pattern shows how specialized agents can be orchestrated to handle different aspects of code review in parallel.",
        "execSummary":  "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore is being positioned as the platform layer for embedding AI into enterprise software development workflows — this post is a concrete signal that AWS sees the SDLC as a primary agentic use case, not just customer-facing applications. The two examples (schema documentation and security analysis) address real developer pain points and show that multi-agent orchestration is production-viable today, not a future roadmap item. For enterprise technology leaders, this is a prompt to evaluate where in their own SDLC AI agents can reduce cycle time or improve quality gates — security review is a particularly high-value, low-risk starting point. As with all AgentCore content, this is tightly coupled to the AWS ecosystem and should be evaluated against your existing toolchain before adopting.",
        "vendorLean":  "AWS — built on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore; positions the platform as the hub for AI-assisted software development.",
