        "source":  "CIO.com",
        "url":  "https://www.cio.com/article/4166851/coherence-where-leadership-and-ai-success-intersect.html",
        "date":  "2026-05-07",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "BNY\u0027s CIO Leigh-Ann Russell discusses how \u0027coherence\u0027 as a leadership discipline helps balance innovation with control in enterprise AI deployment. The bank has achieved 220 AI solutions in production, trained over 65% of employees on AI capabilities, and deployed 140 autonomous digital employees working alongside human staff. Russell frames coherence — aligning strategy, culture, and execution — as the missing ingredient in most failed enterprise AI programs.",
        "execSummary":  "BNY\u0027s production metrics — 220 AI solutions, 65% workforce AI-trained, 140 autonomous digital employees — represent one of the most credible at-scale enterprise AI deployments on record, making this a high-value benchmark for any organization assessing its own AI maturity. The coherence framework Russell describes is essentially a discipline for ensuring that AI strategy, organizational culture, change management, and execution are mutually reinforcing rather than working at cross-purposes — the root cause of most enterprise AI program failures. For senior leaders, the practical takeaway is that AI deployment at scale is as much a people and alignment problem as a technology problem, and that investment in workforce enablement is not optional — it is the precondition for agent deployment to succeed. The caveat is that BNY\u0027s resources and regulatory clarity give it advantages most enterprises do not have, so the specific metrics should be contextualized rather than directly benchmarked.",
        "vendorLean":  "Neutral",
