        "date":  "2026-09-04",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Deloitte launched its Open Model Engineering practice to help enterprises adopt a hybrid AI approach combining proprietary and open-source models. The practice initially focuses on Nvidia\u0027s Nemotron models and will hire and train forward-deployed engineers through 2027 across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific. It addresses enterprise challenges including model selection, cost prediction, data sovereignty, and IP protection.",
        "execSummary":  "Deloitte is productizing the hybrid AI stack decision that most enterprises are struggling to make on their own — specifically which mix of frontier and open-source models to run, and how to operationalize that choice securely. The launch arrives alongside Nvidia\u0027s $12.9B Hugging Face acquisition, signaling that the open-model ecosystem is maturing fast enough to attract both chip giants and advisory firms. For enterprise leaders, the practical implication is that selecting a model strategy is now a procurement and governance decision, not just an engineering one. Watch for lock-in risk: deep reliance on a single SI\u0027s model engineering practice could limit flexibility as the landscape shifts.",
        "vendorLean":  "Deloitte — the article frames Deloitte\u0027s new practice as a solution to a real enterprise problem, with expert quotes from Deloitte\u0027s own global AI leader.",
